<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil slips, buyers hold back.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil slips, buyers hold back.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.6864)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p>HAMBURG	     35.30/35.80     20.93/21.23     35.40/35.90</p>
<p>BREMEN		35.30/35.80     20.93/21.23     35.40/35.90</p>
<p>DUISBURG	    35.40/35.90     20.99/21.29     35.30/35.80</p>
<p>FRANKFURT	   36.20/36.50     21.47/21.64     36.30/36.60</p>
<p>KARLSRUHE	   36.30/36.60     21.53/21.70     36.40/36.70</p>
<p>INGOLSTADT	  37.60/37.90     22.30/22.47     37.70/38.20</p>
<p>German inland gas oil was a touch easier on Friday, but buyers were still not being attracted and prices may have to lose up to 20 pfenning more, traders said. Mild temperatures were giving no buying pressure.-- London +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
